>TACHINO, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HANEDA YASUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAYASHI NAHOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MICHIHATA KEIZO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMO HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TACHINO HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HANEDA, YASUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAYASHI, NAHOTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MICHIHATA, KEIZO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMO, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TACHINO, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A molded part manufactured by blending or laminating a barrier resin having a solubility parameter (calculated from the Fedors equation) over 11 and a thermoplastic resin having a solubility parameter (calculated from the Fedors equation) under 11. The molded part is excellent in gasoline barrier properties, thermal fusibility and mechanical strength. A fuel container (2) provided with the molded part (1) is drastically improved in leakage of fuel from the molded part portion.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une pièce moulée, fabriquée par mélange ou stratification d'une résine formant une barrière et possédant un paramètre de solubilité (calculé à partir de l'équation de Fedors) supérieur à 11, et d'une résine thermoplastique possédant un paramètre de solubilité (calculé à partir de l'équation de Fedors) inférieur à 11. Cette pièce moulée possède d'excellentes propriétés barrière par rapport à l'essence, de même qu'une thermofusibilité et une résistance mécanique, excellentes. L'invention concerne un réservoir à combustible (2) doté de cette pièce moulée (1), et grandement amélioré sur le plan fuite du combustible à partir de la portion de pièce moulée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>